>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `Dest`

``` hol4
clasetLib.Dest : thm -> thm
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Marks a theorem as an unsafe destruction rule for one tactic invocation.

`Dest th` is logically equivalent to `th`, but a classical tactic recognizes
its marker and adds the theorem to a temporary rule set. A destruction rule
derives consequences from a major premise matched against an assumption and
is converted internally to elimination-rule form. This marker gives it the
unsafe proof-search classification.

The safe classical tactics do not apply unsafe rules. Use `SDest th` to make a
rule available to those tactics. The corresponding argument-free theorem
attribute is `[dest]`; despite its plain spelling it is unsafe. `[sdest]`
registers the safe classification.

### Failure

Constructing `Dest th` does not validate the rule. A tactic that consumes
the marker may fail if `th` has no suitable major premise or cannot be
converted from destruction-rule form to elimination-rule form.

### Example

``` hol4
classicalLib.SAFE_TAC [clasetLib.Dest my_dest_rule]
```

The theorem is accepted as an unsafe rule and is therefore not applied by
`SAFE_TAC`.

